# api — typed API + frontend codegen

This product wires `api.Module(api.Info{...})` and declares its first operation in
`HelloModule`. Declare each operation ONCE in Go; get OpenAPI + a typed client.

```go
api.Handle[Req, Resp]("cameras.get", "GET /cameras/{cam}", fn,
    api.Require("cameras.read"))
```

- Request fields bind from `path:"cam"` / `query:"since"` tags and the JSON body;
  `api.None` = no body/204.
- Failures ride `application/problem+json` (`status`/`code`/`message`/`params`/
  `fields`/`trace_id`/`retryable`). Return `api.Errorf(404, ...)` for quick sugar,
  `api.Fail(409, "zone.overlaps", ...).Params(...)` for a stable domain code,
  `api.Invalid(api.Field(...))` for a 422; declare mapped domain errors per op with
  `api.MapErr[*T](status, code)`. 5xx is redacted (detail to the log + trace).
- `api.Websocket[Send, Recv](name, path)` declares realtime contracts.
- `go run . openapi` emits OpenAPI 3.1 (error responses carry `x-error-codes`);
  `go run . client --out src/lib/api` generates the Svelte client as per-resource
  modules: `common.ts`, `errors.keys.ts`, `<resource>/{types,client,queries,streams}.ts`,
  `index.ts`. TanStack option factories (`getHelloQuery()` etc.) compose with caller
  overrides. `@tanstack/svelte-query` is the only peer.

